  "explanation": {
    "short": "A dead syllable that starts with a low-class letter has a high tone if its vowel is short (รัก, วัด, นก, รถ) and a falling tone if its vowel is long (ลูก, มาก, ชอบ). With a high-class letter, a dead syllable is simply low (สิบ).",
    "more": "This completes the system. Mid class: live syllables are mid, dead syllables are low. High class: live syllables rise, dead syllables are low. Low class: live syllables are mid; dead ones are high when short and falling when long. The marks ่ and ้ then override all of this, as you learned. The word ครับ follows the rule too: a low-class ค, a short vowel and a closing p make it high."
  },
